# Client-side configuration for the Mail and Vault apps.
#
# Both of these are PUBLIC identifiers, not secrets. Vite inlines any VITE_*
# variable into the JavaScript bundle, so they are readable by anyone who opens
# devtools — which is fine, because neither grants access on its own:
#
#   · the Convex URL only addresses the deployment; every function checks auth
#   · the Clerk key is a *publishable* key, designed to ship in browser code
#
# What actually gates access is the address allowlist in personal-os's
# convex/users.ts. Nothing here weakens it.
#
# Mirror these into Vercel with:
#   vercel env add VITE_CONVEX_URL production
#   vercel env add VITE_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY production

VITE_CONVEX_URL=https://combative-grouse-546.convex.cloud
VITE_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_c3BsZW5kaWQtc3F1aWQtNDguY2xlcmsuYWNjb3VudHMuZGV2JA
